[
    {
        "content": "<p>Dear All,</p>\n<p>I ran into the following quirky behaviour of <code>show_term</code>: the <code>Try this</code> suggestion consumes all the \"syntactic tail\" of the consumed tactic sequence, instead of just the tactics that it should replace.  Here are a couple of examples.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"sd\">/--</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">info: Try this:</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  [apply] exact True.intro</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">constructor</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">show_term</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">trivial</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">trivial</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- The replacement *does not* keep this</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/--</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">info: Try this:</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  [apply] exact True.intro</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">constructor</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">show_term</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">trivial</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">trivial</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- The replacement keeps this</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- Similar behaviour, just more lines</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">constructor</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">show_term</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">trivial</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">refine</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- The replacement *does not* keep this</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">skip</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">skip</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">skip</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">skip</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">skip</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">skip</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">skip</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">skip</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">skip</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">trivial</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">done</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 608222564,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1783200136
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It's hard to say how it should really do this though since <code>show_term</code> takes the entire remaining tactic sequence as input (unless you provide the tactic inline). So you can compare it to</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">constructor</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">show_term</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">trivial</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">refine</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?_;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">trivial</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">done</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>In this case I think it's much less obvious what <em>should</em> happen and how. Perhaps <code>show_term</code> should produce one term for each goal that was operated on instead of just the main goal? Or maybe it should just give an error?</p>",
        "id": 608222826,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1783200487
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I agree that it is not easy to find a good alternative.  I had just not observed this behaviour before.  Honestly, I probably prefer the current behaviour to an error.</p>",
        "id": 608222981,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1783200667
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Maybe, your suggestion of emitting one <code>exact ...</code> per goal would be better, though.</p>",
        "id": 608223117,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1783200811
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Probably I'm saying nothing that is not already known, but with proper indentation this works correctly:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">constructor</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">show_term</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">trivial</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">trivial</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I agree with Robin that if <code>show_term</code> gets a tactic sequence that operates on multiple goals, it should probably give replacement text for all goals (though it sounds finicky to produce a tactic script that always does the right thing).</p>",
        "id": 608406593,
        "sender_full_name": "Floris van Doorn",
        "timestamp": 1783331712
    }
]